{0 Rate limiting}

{!Workero.Rate_limiter} is the
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/rate-limit/}Workers Rate Limiting}
binding. The limit and the period belong to the binding, not to the code.

{1 Configure}

[namespace_id] is a number that you pick. Bindings with the same [namespace_id]
share their counters:

{@toml[
[[ratelimits]]
name = "LIMITER"
namespace_id = "1001"
simple = { limit = 100, period = 60 }
]}

[period] is 10 or 60 seconds.

{1 Use}

{@ocaml[
let handler req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  let limiter = Rate_limiter.of_env env "LIMITER" in
  let key = Option.value (Request.header req "cf-connecting-ip") ~default:"anonymous" in
  if Rate_limiter.limit limiter key then Response.text "ok\n"
  else Response.text ~status:`Too_Many_Requests "slow down\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

- {!Workero.Rate_limiter.of_env} opens the binding. It raises
  [Invalid_argument] when there is no such binding, or when the binding has no
  [limit] method.
- {!Workero.Rate_limiter.limit} counts one request for the key and returns
  [true] when it is allowed. Choose a key that identifies who you limit, such
  as a user id or an IP address, not the whole URL.

The count is local to the location that runs the Worker and is eventually
consistent, so treat the limit as approximate.

{1 Test}

The binding is not available in a plain [workerd] configuration. The tests of
workero use a stub that implements [limit] and wraps it as a binding. See
[test/worker/services/limiter.mjs].
